{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.sjny.edu/alumni/career-services": {
      "title": "Lifetime Career Services for Alumni",
      "description": "Career Services | Alumni Services  | \n                  \n                       St. Joseph's University, New York Skip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\". Ready . Set . J oe ’ s MySJNY Apply Menu Accessible Menu - Main Menu Home About Back About Fast Facts Mission History Accreditation Digital Accessibility Policy Public Relations Student Right to Know Academics Back Academics Brooklyn Programs by Department Brooklyn Academic Programs Search Long Island Programs by Department Long Island Academic Program Search Online Academic Programs Undecided Students Summer Sessions Commencement News Leadership Back Leadership President's Office President's Cabinet Office of the Provost Board of Trustees Organizational Chart Directory Library Alumni Back Alumni Make a Gift Events SJNYconnect Mentor Program Lifetime Career Services Virtual Book Club Meet the Staff Resources Back Resources 25-26 Academic Calendar 26-27 Academic Calendar Bursar Emergency Management Employment Institutional Review Board I.T. Services Marketing and Communications Offices Request Transcript Security Menu Brooklyn Back Brooklyn Programs and Departments Admissions Student Life Military & Veterans Athletics Events Long Island Back Long Island Programs and Departments Admissions Student Life Military & Veterans Athletics Events Online Back Online Programs Admissions FAQ Affordability Military & Veterans Alumni > Lifetime Career Services Lifetime Career Services for Alumni Whether you are a recent graduate looking for your first job or an experienced alumni ready to make a career change, our Office of Career Preparation and Professional Development can work with you to achieve your continuing career goals. 1:1 appointments are scheduled either in person or by phone where we can support your individual needs. Services Whatever career move you are planning next, we may be a potential support for you. We can assist with: Career transitions Preparing your job search materials Résumé and cover letter critiques Mock interviews Review of your online presence Access to our online job board Handshake Applying to graduate programs Request Access to Handshake Today! For alumni access to Handshake please send an email to sjcareers@sjny.edu . Please include, your name, year you graduated, and the email address you would like to use for your account. Tip: Use a simple email address that you check regularly. For example: firstname.last name@gmail.com) Post Internship/Job Opportunities Alumni can be a valuable source for networking, full-time job leads and internships, allowing students to explore careers and gain practical work experience. Similarly, the current student community is a potential source of talent for your organization. Posting opportunities is free! For access to Handshake please send an email to: sjcareers@sjny.edu . Handshake is available to all current students and alumni of St. Joseph's University, with the ability to post part-time, full-time, entry-level and experienced opportunities. On-Campus Recruitment Opportunities On-campus recruitment is an excellent way to build your presence on campus and attract highly qualified students. This can be done primarily through: Information Table The Office of Career Preparation and Professional Development invites employers to visit campus and host an Information Table in a high-traffic area, informing students about opportunities available with your organization. Career Fairs Career Fairs are offered at least once a year on both campuses. Employers from various fields are invited to participate and meet with students to share organizational information and opportunities for employment, internships or volunteering. Please email sjcareers@sjny.edu or visit the Office of Career Preparation and Professional Development page at the links below to learn more about these opportunities. Refer Employers If you meet with clients or colleagues who may have an interest in recruiting our students, please feel free to refer their name and contact information to a member of our career team for follow-up. If your company/organization has current internships or jobs available, have your human resources representative email us at sjcareers@sjny.edu or call one of our career office at 631.687.1248 (Long Island campus) or 718.940.5887 (Brooklyn campus). Contact Career Services Brooklyn Visit Brooklyn Career Services Long Island and Online Visit Long Island and Online Career Services Brooklyn Campus Career Services Long Island Campus Career Services Alumni Association Alumni Benefits Athletic Hall of Fame Request an Official Transcript St. Joseph’s On Social Alumni Grant Application Alumni Directory Project Has your information changed? UPDATE INFO Get Social Get Social Esse non videri — “To be, not to seem.” The mission of St. Joseph’s University is to provide a strong academic and value-oriented education at the undergraduate and graduate levels, rooted in a liberal arts tradition that supports provision for career preparation and enhancement. READ OUR FULL MISSION. BROOKLYN 245 Clinton Ave., Brooklyn, NY 11205 Addess For - BROOKLYN Main: 718.940.5300 Admissions: 718.940.5800 Fax: 718.940.5680 Home About Admissions Academics Student Life Library Athletics Alumni Giving MySJNY Privacy Policy LONG ISLAND 155 W. Roe Blvd., Patchogue, NY 11772 Addess For - LONG ISLAND Main: 631.687.5100 Admissions: 631.687.4500 Fax: 631.687.4539 Home About Admissions Academics Student Life Library Athletics Alumni Giving MySJNY Privacy Policy ONLINE 155 W. Roe Blvd., Patchogue, NY 11772 Addess For - ONLINE 631.687.4501 Home Programs Admissions FAQs Affordability Credit for Experience Military & Veterans Library Privacy Policy Sitemap | Accessibility Statement Opens in new window PDF Download Word Download Excel Download PowerPoint Download Document Download Explore your accessibility options"
    },
    "https://www.sjny.edu/employment/job/11025": {
      "title": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor — Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor — Nursing | \n                  \n                       St. Joseph's University, New York Skip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\". Ready . Set . J oe ’ s MySJNY Apply Menu Accessible Menu - Main Menu Home About Back About Fast Facts Mission History Accreditation Digital Accessibility Policy Public Relations Student Right to Know Academics Back Academics Brooklyn Programs by Department Brooklyn Academic Programs Search Long Island Programs by Department Long Island Academic Program Search Online Academic Programs Undecided Students Summer Sessions Commencement News Leadership Back Leadership President's Office President's Cabinet Office of the Provost Board of Trustees Organizational Chart Directory Library Alumni Back Alumni Make a Gift Events SJNYconnect Mentor Program Lifetime Career Services Virtual Book Club Meet the Staff Resources Back Resources 25-26 Academic Calendar 26-27 Academic Calendar Bursar Emergency Management Employment Institutional Review Board I.T. Services Marketing and Communications Offices Request Transcript Security Menu Brooklyn Back Brooklyn Programs and Departments Admissions Student Life Military & Veterans Athletics Events Long Island Back Long Island Programs and Departments Admissions Student Life Military & Veterans Athletics Events Online Back Online Programs Admissions FAQ Affordability Military & Veterans Adjunct Clinical Instructor — Nursing September 3, 2026 Brooklyn Campus Nursing The Adjunct Clinical Instructor will be responsible for delivering high-quality clinical education to nursing students at the undergraduate levels in the field at their clinical location sites. Qualifications Strong background in Nursing and Nursing Education ·Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Commitment to student development and academic excellence Must hold a Masters in Nursing Current and unrestricted RN license in NYS Prior clinical teaching experience in a higher education setting Application Process and Additional Information Salary: $80.00 hourly per semester, per clinical contract hours The university does not sponsor H1-B visas. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Cover letters and resumes can be emailed to: Dr. Giannakas-Lafaro, Executive Director of Nursing, agiannakas@sjny.edu Mail For - Application Process and Additional Information . It is the policy of St. Joseph's University not to discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex,\n  national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, citizenship, age, disability,\n  genetic information, status as a victim of domestic violence, military status, status as a protected\n  veteran, marital status or status of an individual in any group or class protected by applicable federal,\n  New York State or New York City Law. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment,\n  educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, and all other school administered programs or\n  policies. The University also provides accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in accordance\n  with the Americans With Disabilities Act and applicable state and local laws. If you need an\n  accommodation during the application process or while employed, please contact Human Resources. Your employment is contingent upon receipt of proof of eligibility to work in the United States.  Please note that the\n  Department of Homeland Security (DHS) requires that all U.S. employers complete and retain a current Form I-9 for each individual\n  they hire for employment in the United States, verifying the employment eligibility and identity documents presented by the employee\n  and recording the document information.  You will be required to complete your portion of the document, with your documentation verifying\n  your identity and eligibility to work, no later than your third day of employment. Get Social Get Social Esse non videri — “To be, not to seem.” The mission of St. Joseph’s University is to provide a strong academic and value-oriented education at the undergraduate and graduate levels, rooted in a liberal arts tradition that supports provision for career preparation and enhancement. READ OUR FULL MISSION. BROOKLYN 245 Clinton Ave., Brooklyn, NY 11205 Addess For - BROOKLYN Main: 718.940.5300 Admissions: 718.940.5800 Fax: 718.940.5680 Home About Admissions Academics Student Life Library Athletics Alumni Giving MySJNY Privacy Policy LONG ISLAND 155 W. Roe Blvd., Patchogue, NY 11772 Addess For - LONG ISLAND Main: 631.687.5100 Admissions: 631.687.4500 Fax: 631.687.4539 Home About Admissions Academics Student Life Library Athletics Alumni Giving MySJNY Privacy Policy ONLINE 155 W. Roe Blvd., Patchogue, NY 11772 Addess For - ONLINE 631.687.4501 Home Programs Admissions FAQs Affordability Credit for Experience Military & Veterans Library Privacy Policy Sitemap | Accessibility Statement Opens in new window PDF Download Word Download Excel Download PowerPoint Download Document Download Explore your accessibility options"
